Sieve of Eratosthenes using a bytearray, since I got curious about memory use. I'm a retired machinist teaching myself Python.
```python
def primes(n):
    sieve = bytearray([1]) * (n + 1)
    for i in range(2, isqrt(n) + 1):
        if sieve[i]:
            sieve[i*i::i] = bytes(len(range(i*i, n + 1, i)))
    return [i for i in range(2, n + 1) if sieve[i]]
```
